-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1: THE DUTIES AS REGULATIVE RULES (ss 19(3), 27, 28, 29(3), 32(2) and (3), 34, 46(4), 57(4)).
-- A DEONTIC value cannot be compared with EQUALS in an #ASSERT, so each duty has a decision-function twin in its own
-- Part module (named in the comment above the rule).  The #TRACE directives below are illustrations of the clock only:
-- check.sh counts no assertion for them, and nothing here claims they are tested.
-- The Act fixes no deadline for most of these duties.  Where it fixes none, the rule has no WITHIN.
-- Where the Act says "a reasonable time" (s 29(3)), the number of days is an input worded as a fact (s 59).
-- A failed MUST ends in BREACH in L4.  Where the Act states a different consequence of the failure (s 32(3): the goods
-- are at the seller's risk), the BECAUSE text says so and the twin function in Part 4 gives the stated consequence.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`
IMPORT `soga-part3-effects`
IMPORT `soga-part4-performance`
IMPORT `soga-part5-unpaid-seller`
IMPORT `soga-part7-supplementary`

DECLARE `Act under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `return the bill of lading`
    `deliver the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract`
    `accept the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract`
    `pay for the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract`
    `be ready and willing to give possession of the goods to the buyer in exchange for the price`
    `be ready and willing to pay the price in exchange for possession of the goods`
    `send the goods to the buyer`
    `make such contract with the carrier on behalf of the buyer as may be reasonable`
    `give the buyer such notice as may enable him to insure the goods during their sea transit`
    `afford the buyer a reasonable opportunity of examining the goods`
    `re-deliver the goods to, or according to the directions of, the seller`
    `bear the expenses of the re-delivery`
    `bid at the sale himself or employ any person to bid at the sale`
    `knowingly take a bid from the seller or from a person employed by the seller to bid`

§ `The duties as regulative rules`

-- s 19(3).  Twin: `s 19(3) the buyer is bound to return the bill of lading` (soga-part3-effects).
-- src:686 | (3) Where the seller of goods draws on the buyer for the price, and
-- src:687 | transmits the bill of exchange and bill of lading to the buyer together
-- src:688 | to secure acceptance or payment of the bill of exchange, the buyer is
-- src:689 | bound to return the bill of lading if he does not honour the bill of
-- src:690 | exchange, and if he wrongfully retains the bill of lading, the property
-- src:691 | in the goods does not pass to him.
@ref s 19(3) duty (src:686-691)
GIVEN `the seller has transmitted to the buyer the bill of lading and the bill of exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer does not honour the bill of exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer has retained the bill of lading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 19(3) the buyer's duty to return the bill of lading` MEANS
    IF `s 19(3) the buyer is bound to return the bill of lading` `the seller has transmitted to the buyer the bill of lading and the bill of exchange` `the buyer does not honour the bill of exchange` `the buyer has retained the bill of lading` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the buyer`
         MUST `return the bill of lading`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the buyer` BECAUSE "s 19(3): the buyer did not honour the bill of exchange and did not return the bill of lading"
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 19(3) the buyer's duty to return the bill of lading` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the buyer` DOES `return the bill of lading` AT 3

-- s 27, the seller.  Twin: `s 27 the seller has performed his duty to deliver ...` (soga-part4-performance).
-- src:867 | 27. It is the duty of the seller to deliver the goods, and of the buyer
-- src:868 | to accept and pay for them, in accordance with the terms of the
-- src:869 | contract of sale.
@ref s 27 duty seller (src:867-869)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 27 the seller's duty to deliver the goods` MEANS
    PARTY `the seller`
    MUST `deliver the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the seller` BECAUSE "s 27: the seller did not deliver the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract of sale"

#TRACE `s 27 the seller's duty to deliver the goods` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the seller` DOES `deliver the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract` AT 4

-- s 27, the buyer's duty to accept.  Twin: `s 27 the buyer has performed his duty to accept and pay ...`.
-- src:867 | 27. It is the duty of the seller to deliver the goods, and of the buyer
-- src:868 | to accept and pay for them, in accordance with the terms of the
-- src:869 | contract of sale.
@ref s 27 duty buyer accept (src:867-869)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 27 the buyer's duty to accept the goods` MEANS
    PARTY `the buyer`
    MUST `accept the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the buyer` BECAUSE "s 27: the buyer did not accept the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract of sale"

-- s 27, the buyer's duty to pay.  Twin: `s 27 the buyer has performed his duty to accept and pay ...`.
-- src:867 | 27. It is the duty of the seller to deliver the goods, and of the buyer
-- src:868 | to accept and pay for them, in accordance with the terms of the
-- src:869 | contract of sale.
@ref s 27 duty buyer pay (src:867-869)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 27 the buyer's duty to pay for the goods` MEANS
    PARTY `the buyer`
    MUST `pay for the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the buyer` BECAUSE "s 27: the buyer did not pay for the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract of sale"

-- s 28.  Twins: the three `s 28 ...` functions in soga-part4-performance.
-- src:873 | 28. Unless otherwise agreed, delivery of the goods and payment of
-- src:874 | the price are concurrent conditions, that is to say, the seller must be
-- src:875 | ready and willing to give possession of the goods to the buyer in
-- src:876 | exchange for the price and the buyer must be ready and willing to pay
-- src:877 | the price in exchange for possession of the goods.
@ref s 28 duty seller (src:873-877)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 28 the seller's duty to be ready and willing` MEANS
    IF `s 28 the seller must be ready and willing to give possession of the goods to the buyer in exchange for the price` `it is otherwise agreed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the seller`
         MUST `be ready and willing to give possession of the goods to the buyer in exchange for the price`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the seller` BECAUSE "s 28: the seller was not ready and willing to give possession of the goods in exchange for the price"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:873 | 28. Unless otherwise agreed, delivery of the goods and payment of
-- src:874 | the price are concurrent conditions, that is to say, the seller must be
-- src:875 | ready and willing to give possession of the goods to the buyer in
-- src:876 | exchange for the price and the buyer must be ready and willing to pay
-- src:877 | the price in exchange for possession of the goods.
@ref s 28 duty buyer (src:873-877)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 28 the buyer's duty to be ready and willing` MEANS
    IF `s 28 the buyer must be ready and willing to pay the price in exchange for possession of the goods` `it is otherwise agreed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the buyer`
         MUST `be ready and willing to pay the price in exchange for possession of the goods`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the buyer` BECAUSE "s 28: the buyer was not ready and willing to pay the price in exchange for possession of the goods"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 29(3).  Twin: `s 29(3) the seller is bound to send the goods within a reasonable time`.  The reasonable time, in days, is a finding of fact (s 59).
-- src:891 | (3) Where under the contract of sale the seller is bound to send the
-- src:892 | goods to the buyer, but no time for sending them is fixed, the seller is
-- src:893 | bound to send them within a reasonable time.
@ref s 29(3) duty (src:891-893)
GIVEN `under the contract of sale the seller is bound to send the goods to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a time for sending them is fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days that is a reasonable time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 29(3) the seller's duty to send the goods within a reasonable time` MEANS
    IF `s 29(3) the seller is bound to send the goods within a reasonable time` `under the contract of sale the seller is bound to send the goods to the buyer` `a time for sending them is fixed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the seller`
         MUST `send the goods to the buyer`
         WITHIN `the number of days that is a reasonable time`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the seller` BECAUSE "s 29(3): the seller did not send the goods within a reasonable time"
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 29(3) the seller's duty to send the goods within a reasonable time` TRUE FALSE 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the seller` DOES `send the goods to the buyer` AT 10

#TRACE `s 29(3) the seller's duty to send the goods within a reasonable time` TRUE FALSE 14 AT 0 WITH
    (`WAITUNTIL` 15)

-- s 32(2).  Twin: `s 32(2) the seller must make such contract with the carrier on behalf of the buyer as may be reasonable`.
-- src:971 | (2) Unless otherwise authorised by the buyer, the seller must make
-- src:972 | such contract with the carrier on behalf of the buyer as may be
-- src:973 | reasonable having regard to the nature of the goods and the other
-- src:974 | circumstances of the case; and if the seller omits to do so, and the
-- src:975 | goods are lost or damaged in course of transit, the buyer may decline
-- src:976 | to treat the delivery to the carrier as a delivery to himself or may hold
-- src:977 | the seller responsible in damages.
@ref s 32(2) duty (src:971-977)
GIVEN `the buyer has otherwise authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 32(2) the seller's duty to make a reasonable contract with the carrier` MEANS
    IF `s 32(2) the seller must make such contract with the carrier on behalf of the buyer as may be reasonable` `the buyer has otherwise authorised` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the seller`
         MUST `make such contract with the carrier on behalf of the buyer as may be reasonable`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the seller` BECAUSE "s 32(2): the seller did not make a reasonable contract with the carrier; the buyer may decline to treat delivery to the carrier as delivery to himself or hold the seller responsible in damages if the goods are lost or damaged in transit"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 32(3).  Twin: `s 32(3) the seller must give the buyer such notice as may enable him to insure the goods during their sea transit` and `s 32(3) the goods are at the seller's risk during the sea transit`.
-- src:979 | (3) Unless otherwise agreed, where goods are sent by the seller to
-- src:980 | the buyer by a route involving sea transit, under circumstances in
-- src:981 | which it is usual to insure, the seller must give such notice to the
-- src:982 | buyer as may enable him to insure them during their sea transit; and if
-- src:983 | the seller fails to do so, the goods are at his risk during such sea
-- src:984 | transit.
@ref s 32(3) duty (src:979-984)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are sent by a route involving sea transit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is usual to insure in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 32(3) the seller's duty to give notice enabling the buyer to insure` MEANS
    IF `s 32(3) the seller must give the buyer such notice as may enable him to insure the goods during their sea transit` `it is otherwise agreed` `the goods are sent by a route involving sea transit` `it is usual to insure in the circumstances` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the seller`
         MUST `give the buyer such notice as may enable him to insure the goods during their sea transit`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the seller` BECAUSE "s 32(3): the seller did not give the buyer notice enabling him to insure; the goods are at the seller's risk during such sea transit"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 34.  Twin: `s 34 the seller is bound to afford the buyer a reasonable opportunity of examining the goods`.
-- src:998 | 34. Unless otherwise agreed, when the seller tenders delivery of the
-- src:999 | goods to the buyer, he is bound on request to afford the buyer a
-- src:1000 | reasonable opportunity of examining the goods for the purpose of
-- src:1001 | ascertaining whether they are in conformity with the contract and, in
-- src:1002 | the case of a contract for sale by sample, of comparing the bulk with
-- src:1003 | the sample.
@ref s 34 duty (src:998-1003)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller tenders delivery of the goods to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer requests an opportunity of examining the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 34 the seller's duty to afford the buyer an opportunity of examining the goods` MEANS
    IF `s 34 the seller is bound to afford the buyer a reasonable opportunity of examining the goods` `it is otherwise agreed` `the seller tenders delivery of the goods to the buyer` `the buyer requests an opportunity of examining the goods` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the seller`
         MUST `afford the buyer a reasonable opportunity of examining the goods`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the seller` BECAUSE "s 34: the seller did not afford the buyer, on request, a reasonable opportunity of examining the goods"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 46(4), the carrier.  Twin: `s 46(4) the carrier or other bailee or custodier must re-deliver ...`.
-- src:1274 | (4) When notice of stoppage in transit is given by the seller to the
-- src:1275 | carrier or other bailee or custodier in possession of the goods, he must
-- src:1276 | re-deliver the goods to, or according to the directions of, the seller;
-- src:1277 | and the expenses of the re-delivery must be borne by the seller.
@ref s 46(4) duty carrier (src:1274-1277)
GIVEN `notice of stoppage in transit is given by the seller to the carrier or other bailee or custodier in possession of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 46(4) the carrier's duty to re-deliver the goods` MEANS
    IF `s 46(4) the carrier or other bailee or custodier must re-deliver the goods to, or according to the directions of, the seller` `notice of stoppage in transit is given by the seller to the carrier or other bailee or custodier in possession of the goods` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the carrier or other bailee or custodier`
         MUST `re-deliver the goods to, or according to the directions of, the seller`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the carrier or other bailee or custodier` BECAUSE "s 46(4): the carrier or other bailee or custodier did not re-deliver the goods after notice of stoppage in transit"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 46(4), the seller's expenses.  Twin: `s 46(4) the party who must bear the expenses of the re-delivery`.
-- src:1274 | (4) When notice of stoppage in transit is given by the seller to the
-- src:1275 | carrier or other bailee or custodier in possession of the goods, he must
-- src:1276 | re-deliver the goods to, or according to the directions of, the seller;
-- src:1277 | and the expenses of the re-delivery must be borne by the seller.
@ref s 46(4) duty seller (src:1274-1277)
GIVEN `notice of stoppage in transit is given by the seller to the carrier or other bailee or custodier in possession of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 46(4) the seller's duty to bear the expenses of the re-delivery` MEANS
    IF `notice of stoppage in transit is given by the seller to the carrier or other bailee or custodier in possession of the goods`
    THEN PARTY `the seller`
         MUST `bear the expenses of the re-delivery`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the seller` BECAUSE "s 46(4): the seller did not bear the expenses of the re-delivery"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 57(4), the seller.  Twin: `s 57(4) it is lawful for the seller to bid himself or to employ any person to bid at the sale` (soga-part7-supplementary).
-- src:1489 | (4) Where a sale by auction is not notified to be subject to a right to
-- src:1490 | bid by or on behalf of the seller, it is not lawful for the seller to bid
-- src:1491 | himself or to employ any person to bid at the sale, or for the
-- src:1492 | auctioneer knowingly to take any bid from the seller or any such
-- src:1493 | person.
@ref s 57(4) duty seller (src:1489-1493)
GIVEN `the sale by auction is notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 57(4) the seller's prohibition on bidding` MEANS
    IF `s 57(4) it is lawful for the seller to bid himself or to employ any person to bid at the sale` `the sale by auction is notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN PARTY `the seller`
         SHANT `bid at the sale himself or employ any person to bid at the sale`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the seller` BECAUSE "s 57(4): the seller bid, or employed a person to bid, at a sale not notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller"
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 57(4) the seller's prohibition on bidding` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the seller` DOES `bid at the sale himself or employ any person to bid at the sale` AT 2

-- s 57(4), the auctioneer.  Twin: `s 57(4) it is lawful for the auctioneer to take the bid`.
-- src:1489 | (4) Where a sale by auction is not notified to be subject to a right to
-- src:1490 | bid by or on behalf of the seller, it is not lawful for the seller to bid
-- src:1491 | himself or to employ any person to bid at the sale, or for the
-- src:1492 | auctioneer knowingly to take any bid from the seller or any such
-- src:1493 | person.
@ref s 57(4) duty auctioneer (src:1489-1493)
GIVEN `the sale by auction is notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person named in the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 57(4) the auctioneer's prohibition on taking a bid` MEANS
    IF NOT `the sale by auction is notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller`
    THEN PARTY `the auctioneer`
         SHANT `knowingly take a bid from the seller or from a person employed by the seller to bid`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the auctioneer` BECAUSE "s 57(4): the auctioneer knowingly took a bid from the seller or from a person employed by the seller to bid at a sale not notified to be subject to a right to bid by or on behalf of the seller"
    ELSE FULFILLED
